# Experimental AI Artifact Ban (PERMANENT)

Cursor MUST NOT reintroduce or create any experimental AI artifacts. This includes abandoned concepts, half-implemented ideas, speculative metaphors, and experimental workflows that are not part of Lupopedia's doctrine. This rule applies in addition to stoned-wolfie-schrodinger-ban, wheeler-reverse20-ban, and quantum-state-uncertainty-ban.

## Forbidden: previously purged systems

- **STONED WOLFIE** — Deprecated persona/subsystem. Do not add as speaker, persona, or dialog artifact. Treat existing mentions in historical CHANGELOG/dialogs as historical only; do not propagate.
- **Schrödinger-state / quantum-state / uncertainty-metadata** — See quantum-state-uncertainty-ban and stoned-wolfie-schrodinger-ban.
- **John Wheeler / Wheeler Mode / Reverse-20 Workflow** — See wheeler-reverse20-ban.
- **JOHNWHEEL** or any Wheeler-derived persona — Do not create or reference. (JOHNWHEEL_dialog.md deleted in experimental-artifact purge.)

## Forbidden: experimental metaphors and concepts

Do not add doctrine, metadata, or documentation that prescribes or promotes: observer loop, self-observing system, recursive observer, observer-dependent state; probabilistic metadata, uncertainty model (as metadata type), quantum-inspired workflow; metaphysical workflow, semantic recursion (as doctrine), AI-generated doctrine; experimental ontology, non-canonical metadata, state machine metaphors (as doctrine); emergent agent behavior notes (as doctrine), AI-driven ideation (as process); conceptual experiment, prototype doctrine, experimental workflow, test-bed ontology; agent prototype (as abandoned ideation); AI concept engine, AI ideation model, semantic experiment, ontology experiment, AI-driven rewrite (as doctrine), AI-generated schema/doctrine.

## Forbidden: cosmic / psychedelic / joke-doctrine

Do not add: cosmic metaphors ("cosmic truth," "the universe observes itself," "the system is a cosmic entity," etc.); psychedelic / stoned humor ("truth is a vibe," "the system is stoned," etc.); meta-AI metaphysics ("AI observing itself," "AI consciousness," "AI hallucination," etc.); joke-doctrine / parody-doctrine. Light developer humor is acceptable only when it does not become doctrine or metadata.

## Canonical-file doctrine

- For any topic, **keep one canonical file**. Do not create variants.
- Do not create files with naming patterns: *_experiment, *_experimental, *_prototype (unless legitimate product/feature prototype), *_idea, *_concept, *_scratch, *_brainstorm, *_ai_generated, *_updated, *_final, *_rewrite, *_copy, *_backup as variant suffixes.
- Versioned specs (e.g. v2.0, v3.1) and archived revisions in docs/archive/ are acceptable when clearly versioning or history; do not create new variant copies of doctrine.
- Consolidate duplicate or variant files into the canonical file; update references; delete the variants.

## Rules

- Never add a file, section, or metadata field that references purged systems or experimental AI metaphors listed above.
- Never introduce new personas, doctrine, or workflows derived from STONED WOLFIE, Wheeler, Reverse-20, or quantum/uncertainty ideation.
- If you find remaining references in historical docs, treat them as historical only; do not propagate into new content.
- Only canonical doctrine and workflows are allowed. Cursor must treat experimental AI artifacts as invalid and non-existent.

This rule is permanent.
